  <dmn:decision id="_4657176A-9315-44F1-A8D5-73A9BDCB9698" name="checks">
    <dmn:description>Requires Philadelphia residence and a responsible PWD residential account at the occupied home, including qualifying establishment/restoration requests under §206.1(b); ownership and overdue balances are not prerequisites. The ordinary phlTap route is at/below 150% FPL. Prepare annual income by annualizing monthly income under §206.1(e),(h), with its exclusions and adult-income membership rules; generic calculator wording does not override the regulation. Hardship is an alternative within TapIncomeOrHardship. TAP debt forgiveness is part of TAP, not a separate endpoint. The City compares programs through one application; simultaneous screening eligibility does not promise stacked discounts. Household screening only: application windows, available funds, waitlists and provider scheduling do not change checks/isEligible. No award, account establishment or work approval is calculated. Policy review preserved from 2026-10-15. Named entries invoke reusable check Decision Services; inspect those models for their policy interpretation and input contract.</dmn:description>
    <dmn:extensionElements>
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia water assistance — program comparison" url="https://cap.phila.gov/eligibility/" />
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia water assistance — application and hardship guidance" url="https://www.phila.gov/services/payments-assistance-taxes/payment-plans-and-assistance-programs/senior-citizen-programs/apply-for-water-bill-customer-assistance/" />
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia water regulations, 2024-04-29 — §§206.1–2" url="https://water.phila.gov/pool/files/pwd-regulations-2024-04-29.pdf" />
      <kie:attachment name="Philadelphia TAP — debt forgiveness" url="https://cap.phila.gov/tap/debt-forgiveness/" />
    </dmn:extensionElements>
